  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Intro Music**: rare: 9 archived performances [8]\n- **MC**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [8]\n- **Good Intentions**: rare: 6 archived performances [8]\n- **Into - Run Thru**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [8]\n- **Look At You**: rare: 13 archived performances [8]\n- **Outro Music**: earliest performance in the archive; mythic rare: 2 archived performances [8]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **mmj2009-02-04.RodeNT4** (recommended): source not stated; 29 songs; 146 min [1]\n- **mmj2009-02-04.dpa4023**: source not stated; 27 songs; 144 min; rated 5/5 by 5 [2]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Reviewer in Lebanon, Pennsylvania, received the tape from Japan via a fan named GT [5]\n- A floor column masked the speaker, forcing the taper to aim diagonally from the right [2]\n- This recording is the first true 2009 tape online, excluding the New Year's Eve show [6]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **mmj2009-02-04.RodeNT4**: taped by Watanabe Satoshi; transferred by Watanabe Satoshi; source: Rode NT4 > Edirol UA-5 Digi-mod (Digital 44.1kHz, 16Bit) > iriver iHP-120 Rockbox (Digital) > CD wave (Split Tracks) > Sound Forge 8.0 (Fade In, Fade Out) >… [1]\n- **mmj2009-02-04.dpa4023**: taped by Gaku Taniguchi (tapersdelight) aka. HuD; transferred by Gaku Taniguchi (tapersdelight) aka. HuD; source: DPA4023 > Mini-Me > D8(16/48) [2]. Also: Japanese tapers struggled for permission, but eno clamped the mic and provided the setlist [2]",
